{"timestamp": "2025-09-15T13:01:00.589710", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # Check if the item is a primitive. If it is, then we don't need to craft it.\n  # Instead, we should collect it.\n  if item in env.world.cookbook.primitives:\n      return collect(env, item)\n\n  # Check if we have all the required items for crafting.\n  # If not, we need to collect them.\n  required_items = env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(item)\n  for required_item, count in required_items.items():\n      # For each required item, check if we have enough in the inventory.\n      # If not, we need to collect it.\n      if env._current_state.inventory[required_item] < count:\n          return collect(env, required_item)\n\n  # If we have all the required items, we need to go to the workshop\n  # and perform the craft action.\n  workshop_index = env.world.cookbook.recipes[item]['workshop']\n  # Get the position of the workshop\n  workshop_pos = find_entity(env, workshop_index)\n  if not workshop_pos:\n      # If workshop not found, we can't craft, so return empty list\n      return []\n\n  # Move to the workshop\n  actions = []\n  actions.extend(move_to(env, workshop_pos))\n\n  # Perform the craft action\n  actions.append(USE)\n\n  return actions", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
