{"timestamp": "2025-09-15T13:39:47.519023", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # First, we need to check if the item can be crafted by the environment. \n  # If not, return empty list.\n  if item not in env.world.cookbook.index.contents:\n    return []\n\n  # Get the index of the item.\n  item_idx = env.world.cookbook.index.contents[item]\n\n  # Check if we already have the item in inventory.\n  if env._current_state.inventory[item_idx] > 0:\n    return []\n  \n  # Check if the item is a primitive (no recipe needed).\n  if item_idx in env.world.cookbook.primitives:\n    return []\n\n  # Get the recipe for the item.\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes[item_idx]\n\n  # Check if we have all the required ingredients.\n  for ingredient, count in recipe.items():\n    if ingredient == \"_key\":\n      continue\n    if env.world.cookbook.index.contents[ingredient] not in env._current_state.inventory:\n      return []\n\n  # Now, we need to find the workshop where the item can be crafted.\n  workshop_idx = None\n  for workshop, workshop_idx in env.world.cookbook.index.contents.items():\n    if workshop.startswith(\"WORKSHOP\"):\n      workshop_idx = workshop_idx\n      break\n\n  # Get the workshop position.\n  workshop_pos = None\n  for i in range(env._current_state.grid.shape[0]):\n    for j in range(env._current_state.grid.shape[1]):\n      if env._current_state.grid[i, j, workshop_idx] > 0:\n        workshop_pos = (i, j)\n        break\n    if workshop_pos:\n      break\n\n  # If workshop not found, return empty list.\n  if workshop_pos is None:\n    return []\n\n  # Move to the workshop.\n  actions = []\n  # Move to the workshop position.\n  # (We assume a function `move_to` is available to calculate movement actions.)\n  actions.extend(move_to(env, workshop_pos))\n\n  # Perform the USE action.\n  actions.append(craft.USE)\n\n  return actions", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": -1}}
