{"timestamp": "2025-09-15T13:43:14.697932", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # Check if the item is craftable and the required primitives are available\n  # If not, return empty list\n  # If yes, then we need to go to the workshop and craft the item\n\n  # To check if the item is craftable, we can look at the recipe for the item\n  # The recipe for the item tells us the required ingredients and the workshop needed\n  # The workshop is a specific type of workshop (WORKSHOP0, WORKSHOP1, WORKSHOP2)\n\n  # We need to find the workshop index for the workshop type required by the recipe\n  # We can get the workshop index from env.world.workshop_indices\n\n  # We need to find the required ingredients for the item\n  # We can get the required ingredients from env.world.cookbook.recipes[item_index]\n\n  # We need to check if we have all the required ingredients\n  # We can check this by looking at the current inventory\n\n  # If we have all the required ingredients, then we need to go to the workshop\n  # We can use the `move_to_workshop` function to move to the workshop\n  # We can use the `craft_item` function to craft the item at the workshop\n\n  # If we don't have all the required ingredients, then we need to collect them\n  # We can use the `collect_primitives` function to collect the missing ingredients\n\n  # We need to return a list of actions that will craft the item\n  # The actions should be a sequence of moves to the workshop and a USE action\n  # We should not return any actions if the item is not craftable or the required ingredients are not available\n  # We should not return any actions if the workshop is not found\n  return []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
