{"timestamp": "2025-09-15T14:06:23.267053", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # If the item is a primitive, we cannot craft it, so we return an empty list.\n  if item in env.world.cookbook.primitives:\n      return []\n\n  # Check if we have all the primitives required to craft the item.\n  required_primitives = env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(env.world.cookbook.index[item])\n  for primitive, count in required_primitives.items():\n      if env._current_state.inventory[primitive] < count:\n          # If we don't have enough of a primitive, return an empty list.\n          return []\n\n  # Now, we need to go to the workshop to craft the item.\n  # First, find the workshop index for the item (the workshop where it can be crafted).\n  workshop_index = None\n  for workshop, item_list in env.world.cookbook.recipes.items():\n      if item in item_list:\n          workshop_index = workshop\n          break\n\n  if workshop_index is None:\n      # If no workshop found, return empty list.\n      return []\n\n  # Now, find the position of the workshop in the grid.\n  # The workshop is a specific entity type, so we look for its position in the grid.\n  workshop_pos = None\n  for i in range(env.world.world.grid.shape[0]):\n      for j in range(env.world.world.grid.shape[1]):\n          if env.world.world.grid[i, j, workshop_index] > 0:\n              workshop_pos = (i, j)\n              break\n      if workshop_pos:\n          break\n\n  if workshop_pos is None:\n      # If workshop not found, return empty list.\n      return []\n\n  # Now, we need to move to the workshop position.\n  # Calculate the direction to move based on the current position and workshop position.\n  current_pos = env._current_state.pos\n  # Calculate the direction to move to reach the workshop.\n  # The direction is based on the relative position of the workshop.\n  dir_to_workshop = None\n  if workshop_pos[0] > current_pos[0]:\n      dir_to_workshop = \"DOWN\"\n  elif workshop_pos[0] < current_pos[0]:\n      dir_to_workshop = \"UP\"\n  elif workshop_pos[1] > current_pos[1]:\n      dir_to_workshop = \"RIGHT\"\n  elif workshop_pos[1] < current_pos[1]:\n      dir_to_workshop = \"LEFT\"\n\n  # Now, generate the actions to move to the workshop.\n  actions = []\n  if dir_to_workshop == \"UP\":\n      actions.append(1)  # UP\n  elif dir_to_workshop == \"DOWN\":\n      actions.append(0)  # DOWN\n  elif dir_to_workshop == \"LEFT\":\n      actions.append(2)  # LEFT\n  elif dir_to_workshop == \"RIGHT\":\n      actions.append(3)  # RIGHT\n\n  # After moving to the workshop, we need to perform a USE action.\n  actions.append(4)  # USE\n\n  return actions", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
